#: app/qml/HearingNotice.qml:37
msgctxt "@info notice before the first Hearing block; keep the bold tags"
msgid ""
"<b>Keep it comfortable.</b> Sound should never be uncomfortable or painful. "
"If it is, turn it down or take your headphones off. Start with the volume low"
" and raise it slowly."
msgstr "<b>保持舒适。</b>声音绝不应让人感到不适或疼痛。如果出现这种情况，请调低音量或摘下耳机。先从低音量开始，再慢慢调高。"

#: app/qml/HearingNotice.qml:38
msgctxt "@info notice before the first Hearing block; keep the bold tags"
msgid ""
"<b>These limits do not protect your ears.</b> They work on numbers inside the"
" computer. How loud that is at your ear depends on your volume, your sound "
"card and your headphones, which Reverblabr can't know. Long hours of loud "
"sound can harm hearing with no warning."
msgstr ""
"<b>这些限制并不能保护您的耳朵。</b>它们只作用于计算机内部的数值。传到您耳中的声音有多响，取决于您的音量、声卡和耳机，而这些是 Reverblabr"
" 无法得知的。长时间听很响的声音，可能会在毫无预兆的情况下损伤听力。"

#: app/qml/HearingNotice.qml:39
msgctxt "@info notice before the first Hearing block; keep the bold tags"
msgid ""
"<b>Some changes need a doctor, not a setting.</b> See a doctor straight away "
"if your hearing changes suddenly or gets much worse within days, in one ear "
"or both. Time matters. If this comes with a weak or numb face or a spinning "
"feeling, or after a blow to the head, call for emergency help. See a doctor "
"soon if one ear is worse than the other, your hearing comes and goes, you "
"hear ringing in one ear or a beat in time with your pulse, you feel dizzy, or"
" an ear hurts, feels blocked, looks injured or leaks blood, pus or fluid. "
"Ringing that keeps you awake or gets you down is worth a visit too. Don't "
"turn one side up to make up for a change: a setting can hide it."
msgstr ""
"<b>有些变化需要看医生，而不是调设置。</b>如果您的听力突然变化，或在几天内明显变差，无论是单耳还是双耳，请立即就医。时间很关键。如果同时出现面部无力或麻木、天旋地转的感觉，或发生在头部受到撞击之后，请呼叫急救。如果一只耳朵比另一只差，听力时好时坏，一只耳朵有耳鸣或听到与脉搏同步的搏动声，感到头晕，或者耳朵疼痛、有堵塞感、看起来受伤或流出血液、脓液或其他液体，请尽快就医。如果耳鸣让您难以入睡或情绪低落，也值得去看看医生。不要为了弥补变化而调高一侧的音量：设置可能会掩盖问题。"

#: app/qml/HearingNotice.qml:40
msgctxt "@info notice before the first Hearing block; keep the bold tags"
msgid ""
"<b>Before you add gain.</b> Don't add these blocks on top of headphones or "
"earpieces that already shape the sound for you: the gains add up. That holds "
"on loudspeakers too, if you wear such earpieces while you listen. Don't set "
"them up for a child. Don't rely on a session for alarms or calls you must not"
" miss: if it stops, the sound can stop or change. Don't wear closed "
"headphones where you need to hear traffic."
msgstr ""
"<b>在添加增益之前。</b>如果您的耳机或耳塞已经在为您调整声音，请不要再在其上叠加这些模块：增益会累加。如果您在用扬声器收听时戴着这类耳塞，也是如此。不要为儿童设置这些模块。不要依靠会话来接收您绝不能错过的警报或来电：会话一旦停止，声音可能会中断或改变。在需要听到交通声音的地方，不要佩戴封闭式耳机。"

